# Cobham SATCOM / Thrane & Thrane / Viasat BGAN terminal firmware signatures
# Derived from analysis of Explorer 100/110, 500/300, and 710 firmware images
#
# Install: cp cobham_bgan.magic ~/.local/share/radare2/magic/
# Usage:   /m cobham_bgan.magic

# =============================================================================
# TIIF — Thrane & Thrane Image Install Format
# =============================================================================
# Used by Explorer 710, 5075, and newer Linux-based BGAN terminals
# Contains PKCS7-signed manifest + multiple sub-images (kernel, rootfs, app, etc.)
0	string		FIITTIIF	Cobham SATCOM TIIF firmware container
>8	lelong		x		\b, version 0x%08x
>0x20	string		tt:		\b, manifest: %.60s
>0x40	string		tt37		\b, build tag: %.40s
>0x64	string		products=	\b, %.20s

# =============================================================================
# Cobham BGAN .dl firmware archive (Explorer 500/300/700 series)
# =============================================================================
# POSIX tar containing: manifest (CRC32 list), MAIN_CPU (custom header+gzip), 
# dsp/ (DSP images), lua/ (web UI scripts)
# The MAIN_CPU sub-image has a custom header:
0	belong		0xFEDEABBA	Cobham BGAN MAIN_CPU firmware image
>4	belong		0xDEADBEAD	\b, magic2 confirmed
>0x10	string		tt37		\b, build: %.20s
>0x30	string		Build-		\b, tag: %.30s

# =============================================================================
# Cobham BGAN monolithic firmware (.APP — Explorer 100/110)
# =============================================================================
# Flat ARM binary for eCos RTOS, no filesystem
# Identified by the entry point pattern and build strings
0	string		\x00\x00\xa0\xe1	Possible ARM eCos firmware (mov r0, r0 NOP)

# =============================================================================
# BGAN DSP sub-images
# =============================================================================
# Found in dsp/asica/, dsp/asicb/, dsp/rfic02/ directories within .dl archives
# These are raw DSP microcode blobs, typically < 100KB each
# No reliable magic — identified by directory structure and context
